{"id": "EUVD-2026-102292", "enisaUuid": "477f71a5-9c03-3712-8e36-011d330f5c1d", "description": "libmikmod through 3.3.15 contains a global out-of-bounds read vulnerability in the MultiTracker loader MTM_Load() because the module channel count is never clamped. Attackers can supply a crafted .mtm file with a channel count above 32 to read past the static pat array, corrupting track indices and crashing the loading application.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:51", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:27:50", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libmikmod-mtm-imf-loader-oob-read", "https://github.com/sezero/mikmod/blob/6e658155f7e6b394a288dac796ba572634553fad/libmikmod/loaders/load_mtm.c#L257-L261", "https://github.com/sezero/mikmod", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libmikmod-through-3.3.15-out-of-bounds-read-in-mtm-load-via-channel-count"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f5qx-fp8j-qm9m", "CVE-2026-111165"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cfb7a00c-81e2-323f-9c7c-14d7721c1b04", "product": {"name": "libmikmod", "vendor": {"name": "sezero"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.3.15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3e885618-94b7-34b2-9def-d93f44c5538f", "vendor": {"name": "sezero"}}], "isExploited": false}